{"kind":"request","text":"FH-2: the pre-commit hook passes a commit that it has nothing to\ncheck.\n\nThe fact at head 720f228a. `scripts/pre-commit.mjs` refuses each\ncommit in a checkout with no local Prettier, before it reads what the\ncommit stages. `core.hooksPath` is a shared setting, so the hooks\nturn on for every worktree at one time. A planner worktree for a\nsprint report or a design note has no `node_modules`, and it stages\nonly Markdown. With the hooks on, that worktree cannot commit. So the\nhooks stay off today, and FH-1 saves no gate attempt yet.\n\nOutcome: the hooks are on for every worktree, and a notes worktree\ncommits.\n\nWork:\n1. The hook reads the staged paths first. When no staged path is a\n   file that the formatter selects, the hook runs no format check and\n   needs no Prettier.\n2. When no staged path is a file that the shared-helper check scans,\n   the hook does not run that check.\n3. When a staged path needs a check and its tool is missing, the hook\n   refuses as it does today, with the same words.\n4. The commit-msg hook does not change. State in `docs/testing.md`\n   whether it needs `node_modules`.\n5. Named cases in `scripts/git-hooks.test.mjs`: a Markdown-only\n   commit passes with no Prettier. A commit with one selected JSON\n   file and no Prettier refuses. A commit with unformatted JSON\n   refuses, as today.\n\nAfter FH-2 lands, I run `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` in the\nshared repository and file the act.\n\nSide lane. It rides any waiting side head, and it takes no gate\nposition before R, E1 and the NF-6 head.\n\nThis request adds no scope kind, no platform definition name, no\ncapability name or form, no tool family and no record model.","body":{"conditions":"Rides a waiting side head and its gate. Review by the checker. The planner turns the hooks on after the landing.","target_head":"4b198d0fc980327d87347b05a3817106974bf8d7","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f75